<description>&lt;p&gt;Colombia has opened an embassy in Jerusalem and begun a cultural counterrevolution that is removing more than thirty artworks from the National Museum and ordering the removal of LGBTQ2S+ political works. The Mobile Anti-Riot Squad (ESMAD) has returned to operate in the country and an evangelist was killed after refusing to lend a motorcycle to a criminal group in Cartagena. The president is set to sign a decree on the maritime boundaries of the San Andres, Providencia and Santa Catalina Archipelago, while former rebel leaders have been charged with war crimes against Indigenous groups. An earthquake left more than 224 dead and a Colombian asylum seeker was tackled by ICE agents in Washington, and 225 battle-related deaths were recorded in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiuAFBVV95cUxQQ0cwZXpTd2VWakhHY1MtXy1BZl9hNVZ6dTllYmxOeDRESjE1THZUUW03Z0h1clhVOHN2R2t0MHpYcEo5Nk9CY2QtanA3aEYweHJPSHMweTh2NkNsUE9UZjAySmJkbGtaajZhc3ZOX3YySzBXdGV1OF9OdktOYWdtMGE0Y3k0LWNGdy1Eb3U2T3BjNjd6VlhrOXdjU3QtRjRYUFoxUUFwaDFPdV91NmhlRThweThzUGtZ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Diálogo Americas&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Malta Independent Online&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqAFBVV95cUxQakFtMFpXUmp1R2k2ZXVNTTUtTS1QSWx1bjZ6eDdLWG5zcFIxamhUd1lhVVJOOXZaVm5MamM2SkI5VmJ3eEtnRmROMVk2bzJMX182LWY2Nk1xZE11aDlNTWkyWEZaTHZWOTdyRUpiQklnREVqNDZxRzhKRWVxTnNNa2hpUmt5eUFzYTVGZzJ6V0dXUXlMRzFUUms2MWM5SE5lUGh2T2FlVmM?oc=5&quot;&gt;Times of Malta&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivgFBVV95cUxPUTJpbkgtRFhVb2N0WTVfejYyRzNiaWdta1U3T01DbmRQRUxjS2MzSmRYc3NiMG9BM2ZiTnpCb01wQlAycVBEMkcwamsyVmx6VlQ5SEhOYVZXLVotbmVvWFVZOWR0bmc5QXQzNWpoT2YwdWJkRExORUE3cUEzdFd5azg1VXVEVmNHenhWTzlPcXVaR1RxZ29OSVlpd09adFp6aWNiSUFtZjRtTW1UNk1sb